<title>UK: Sakura Bank to buy back dollar convertible bond.</title>
<headline>Sakura Bank to buy back dollar convertible bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sakura Bank Ltd said in a statement on Friday it was offering to buy back a convertible dollar bond issued by Mitsui Bank Ltd.</p>
<p>The bond, issued on March 7, 1988 for $200 million, with a 2.625 percent coupon and due 2003 has $104 million outstanding.</p>
<p>The offer ends July 18 and the bonds will be repurchased at 92 percent of the principal amount of the bonds. -- London Newsroom  +44 171 542 7970</p>
